$-- document-metadata.latex — build shim. Owner: incident-rank-validation preprint build.
$-- pandoc <=3.x shipped a built-in document-metadata.latex partial; pandoc 3.8.2 dropped it,
$-- which breaks the partial reference in arxiv-template.latex. This file reproduces the
$-- last-good (2026-07-02) build, where that reference resolved to empty output. Title,
$-- author, and date are set by arxiv-template.latex itself (\title/\author/\maketitle), so
$-- an empty partial changes nothing in the rendered PDF.
$--
$-- Two rules for editing this file:
$--   1. Use $-- template comments, not % LaTeX comments. pandoc strips the former and
$--      copies the latter into the generated .tex, where it becomes preamble noise in the
$--      arXiv source package.
$--   2. Never write pandoc partial-call syntax here, not even inside a comment. pandoc
$--      renders a partial as a template, so a self-reference expands recursively until it
$--      hits the recursion limit and dumps ~250 duplicated lines into the generated .tex.
